{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401610-how-do-you-express-elder-traits-disciplines-in-v5","id":1401610,"title":"How do you express Elder Traits/Disciplines in V5?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-07-07T20:46:09-07:00","id":1401610,"title":"How do you express Elder Traits/Disciplines in V5?","content":"AFAIK there is no 6+ traits in V5 now and many people have scoffed at this. So how will you express them of older editions in V5?<br /> <br /> My brief thoughts:<br /> 1. Traits: Just like what they had done (Blood Potency, etc.) and Werewolf, raise some new traits and you can add them in your dice pool. Ancestor, Past Life, Renown and so on<br /> <br /> 2. Disciplines:<br /> All level 5-9 disciplines of older editions are folded into the single level 5 and appropriate combo ones, but they are still required something effective (Generation or whatever) to learn, exp you spend depends on the strength, for example (I haven't converted the system):<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2022 Earth Control<br /> Generation (or others) Required: 6<br /> Experience Points Required: as the V5 rules say </div> </div> </div>Of course for me I will modify overpowerful disciplines, making them more reasonable<br /> <br /> Tip:<br /> 1. I will also fold all forms of blood magic(Dur-An-Ki, Koldun, Thaumaturgy, etc.) into the single Blood Sorcery and just leave some options to different ones, making they have more differences in culture or region rather than actual changes<br /> 2. To some Clan or Bloodline Disciplines, I will refine them, making they have more differences in style rather than actual change. For example, I give make Tzimisce Protean, not Vissicitude, but this kind of Protean will appear more &quot;flesh&quot; and &quot;horrible&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T08:35:39-07:00","id":1401696,"title":"","content":"I am still running a V20 game that is part city building and history building to bridge to a V5 game, but here is what I've been mulling over.<br /> <br /> Disciplines: Since the discipline dots are often used in the activation of the powers, I see no reason not to allow this rating to go above 5. Also, many level 6 disciplines have already been retooled to be level 5s now. I think the approach that I will use is that you purchase the Dot rating in a discipline, but can choose the powers up to the dot level you have purchased. Your second dot of a discipline would allow for one level 2 power or two more level 1 powers to the acquired. For elders, this means that their 6th dot can purchase another level 5 and a level 1, or three new level 2s, etc. This will allow for elders to have a width breadth of knowledge of their chosen disciplines, as well as giving them advantage in contested rolls. One of the members of our play group plans to do write ups of new/variant level 6 powers, converting from V20, and depending on how those come out I might use them as well.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24641-sarcasticjazzhands","name":"SarcasticJazzHands","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T13:20:33-07:00","id":1401747,"title":"","content":"I will not adapt those powers because in v5 the idea is to play as neonate struggling to survive. Would be to much pain to homebrew things. Maybe steal the things you like in the v5 lore and use v20 mechanics?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-09T14:53:11-07:00","id":1401972,"title":"","content":"For homebrew, the easiest way to do it without breaking the core system is to build more level 6+ powers as Level 4/5 powers, and use Generation to add how many powers someone can buy. For instance, do it how the LARP and tabletop versions do Generation and Elder junk:<br /> * 8th Gen allows you to buy an additional power of any level, paying appropriate XP costs, in all Disciplines you can learn. 7th makes it 2, 6th makes it 3, 5th makes it 4 and 4th makes it 5, and 4th makes it 6. So janky Methuselahs at 4th Gen have 10 powers in each Discipline at that point, and can buy the homebrewed Level 4 and 5 old elder stuff to fill those last 5 dots worth, depending on how they want to spend their XP. Go for breadth, not height..<br /> <br /> With the basic system, adding dots above 5 adds dice in most instances, which will skew things crazy with the basic way Discipline Power Bonus from Blood Potency works. I posted numbers in another thread with a 7th Gen elder with allowed 7s in stuff trivially getting dice pools into the unbeatable high 20s by default and low-to-mid 30s with trivial effort of surging.<br /> <br /> Even without that, elders are powerful in this system by dint of how much they heal, how much they surge, Rouse rerolls and how much they get bonus dice for DPB from their Blood Potency. You can trivially have the mid teens to low 20s with the right setup and use of Blood Surge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1808,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","user":"elmerg","date":". 07-09-2020, 05:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-10T04:52:24-07:00","id":1402045,"title":"","content":"But above all I don\u2019t disagree that authorities limit all traits up to 5 dots. Advanced powers, especially when the levels are many, are very difficult to write, please see 6+ powers in old editions","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-10T11:16:23-07:00","id":1402093,"title":"","content":"I'm a completionist. There is so much of Cainite history that cannot adapt systematically to V5 (yet) and therefore I'd rather wait until they adapt elders or simply wait 'til V6. I have zero trouble to keep rpging revised/V20 systems.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-10T12:20:31-07:00","id":1402099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401610-how-do-you-express-elder-traits-disciplines-in-v5?p=1402093#post1402093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm a completionist. There is so much of Cainite history that cannot adapt systematically to V5 (yet) and therefore I'd rather wait until they adapt elders or simply wait 'til V6. I have zero trouble to keep rpging revised/V20 systems.<br /> <br /> - Saga</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm curious, what do you believe cannot adapt? Because as it stands, elder rules are in the game. They likely aren't going to get anything special again nor has the lore really relied on the previous 6+ powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24893-necroticbinder","name":"Necroticbinder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-10T12:48:34-07:00","id":1402106,"title":"","content":"To be honest, there are few iconic powers of vampires from folklore and popular culture that can't already be depicted via the existing V5 Disciplines, amalgams, Blood Sorcery rituals, and judicious creativity with loresheets. I don't think 6+ dot disciplines are needed.<br /> <br /> Likewise, the bonus dice to attributes using Blood Surge and discipline rolls in general thanks to Blood Potency largely make up for the lack of 6+ dot Attributes and Skills. Those advantages make elders suitably fearsome compared to neonate characters. I think the system only really fails when you want to depict the vast scope abilities of the antediluvians, and they were relegated to plot device powers in the previous edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-10T14:38:10-07:00","id":1402119,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24641-sarcasticjazzhands\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24641\" data-vbnamecard=\"24641\">SarcasticJazzHands</a> You actually can't just convert a chronicle to V5. Well, like, you can, but players are going to be thinking of stuff like 'that thing I used to be able to do, I can't do it anymore' and they're gonna be sad about it. Suddenly their disciplines are very different (nearly unrecognizable in some cases), their fighting strategies have been upended, the armour they used to wear is useless, their willpower reserve is gone and the points they've put into generation mean a lot less. If you want to take it really far their ghouls have become hopeless...<br /> <br /> (I'll throw it out there; If you wanted to convert a V5 chronicle to V20, you'd have a better time of it; much less to houserule)<br /> <br /> As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24832_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24832\" data-vbnamecard=\"24832\">blailton</a> said, you can take the V5 metaplot you like and it works well with the V20 system, you could take in some things like resonances and houserule in some hunger dice if you wanted,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-10T15:15:27-07:00","id":1402128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401610-how-do-you-express-elder-traits-disciplines-in-v5?p=1402119#post1402119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24641-sarcasticjazzhands\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24641\" data-vbnamecard=\"24641\">SarcasticJazzHands</a> You actually can't just convert a chronicle to V5. Well, like, you can, but players are going to be thinking of stuff like 'that thing I used to be able to do, I can't do it anymore' and they're gonna be sad about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I should speak as a player, that this is something I have done several times already and it's quite fun. Explaining the changes in-universe is a source of WONDERFUL adventure hooks.<br /> <br /> Also, you can just sit down and say, &quot;Okay, everyone, this is the way it's always been. Take note and memorize the changes.&quot;<br /> <br /> So far, everyone has had an ABSOLUTE BLAST and loved it.<br /> <br /> I'm happy to share how I incorporated the changes of V5 in-universe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 07-10-2020, 06:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-10T20:43:29-07:00","id":1402181,"title":"","content":"Elders in V5 are scary because of their blood potency, not the discipline powers themselves. The level-5 discipline powers are nothing to sneeze at, but it's really the fact that elders can use several of them, probably know unexpected amalgam powers because of the number of different disciplines they know, can use many powers at little risk of hunger, can straight-up add a bunch of dice to their already-large discipline pools, and can surge for a bunch more dice if they don't already have to rouse for the discipline power. Sure, maybe you can resist, but they can drown you in successes, often without breaking a sweat.<br /> <br /> But despite that, they're not unbeatable, and that's the key. They don't have automatic &quot;I win&quot; powers. But going up against them directly is probably not a great idea. So the intended dynamic of the young fearing the old, but the old also fearing the young, is represented pretty well.<br /> <br /> So I'd not worry about converting elders in the particulars of their disciplines. The important thing is noting which disciplines they've mastered, and which ones they've branched out into, and especially paying attention to what their blood potency should be for their generation+age. The specific powers you reimagine within the current system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-11T01:39:17-07:00","id":1402201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Necroticbinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401610-how-do-you-express-elder-traits-disciplines-in-v5?p=1402099#post1402099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious, what do you believe cannot adapt? Because as it stands, elder rules are in the game. They likely aren't going to get anything special again nor has the lore really relied on the previous 6+ powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>For starters, Mithras (full strength) in the Fall of London does not feel like he was in previous editions. Someone who could command his entire bloodline but with a thought (Dominate 9 from all editions) or withstand a brawl with Horus for an entire night (London by Night).<br /> <br /> No amount of Oblivion (or an amalgam of it) can represent how Montano physically entered the Abyss and got out through any shadow in the entire world (Lasombra trilogy).<br /> <br /> I don't see how any amount of Blood Sorcery can reflect the might of ur-Shulgi or al-Ashrad since they were both different employments of sorcery to begin with.<br /> <br /> The Dracon going dragon form against Triglav after the embrace and torpor of Gesu (Libellus Sanguinis I + Clanbook Tzimisce revised) is something that might not probably be reflected with Protean 5 (or whatever Vicissitude will become in V5) + Blood Sorcery 5<br /> <br /> Michael's Dreamworld is the most adaptable since it could be considered to be Auspex 5+Dominate 5+Presence 5, yet that means that any neonate who happen to have those levels (unlikely, but possible) could hypothetically do it.<br /> <br /> I won't criticize all the blood magic since V5 is still young and I'm sure something will be upcoming on that, but the task to generalize:<br /> <br /> Blood Sorcery to<br /> - Thaumaturgy<br /> - Dur An Ki<br /> - Akhu<br /> - Sadhana<br /> - Nahuallotl<br /> <br /> and Oblivion to<br /> - Obtenebration<br /> - Necromancy<br /> - Wanga<br /> <br /> is something that might need to be further explained into how can one possibly employ something that it couldn't do before. I personally hope the game the best, but I rather wait until I'm assured that some adaptations I worked for years in my chronicles might actually make a better sense that they do now.<br /> <br /> When Gehenna came out, the book considered Ventrue Antediluvian to be slain right after the Second City, which raised more flame than questions since the writers answers were &quot;errr.... he is beyond life and death&quot; which didn't made sense at all. An &quot;oops, we forgot about Mithras, Alexander and many more embrace dates&quot; would have been better instead of justifying with a lame improvised plot device (that is still being sustained!). Since this things happened before, I rather wait and see that V5 is above such carelessness.<br /> <br /> -Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1594,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","user":"Saga","date":". 07-11-2020, 04:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-11T09:08:59-07:00","id":1402256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401610-how-do-you-express-elder-traits-disciplines-in-v5?p=1402201#post1402201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For starters, Mithras (full strength) in the Fall of London does not feel like he was in previous editions. Someone who could command his entire bloodline but with a thought (Dominate 9 from all editions) or withstand a brawl with Horus for an entire night (London by Night). <br /> <br /> No amount of Oblivion (or an amalgam of it) can represent how Montano physically entered the Abyss and got out through any shadow in the entire world (Lasombra trilogy).<br /> <br /> I don't see how any amount of Blood Sorcery can reflect the might of ur-Shulgi or al-Ashrad since they were both different employments of sorcery to begin with.<br /> <br /> The Dracon going dragon form against Triglav after the embrace and torpor of Gesu (Libellus Sanguinis I + Clanbook Tzimisce revised) is something that might not probably be reflected with Protean 5 (or whatever Vicissitude will become in V5) + Blood Sorcery 5<br /> <br /> Michael's Dreamworld is the most adaptable since it could be considered to be Auspex 5+Dominate 5+Presence 5, yet that means that any neonate who happen to have those levels (unlikely, but possible) could hypothetically do it.<br /> <br /> I won't criticize all the blood magic since V5 is still young and I'm sure something will be upcoming on that, but the task to generalize:<br /> <br /> Blood Sorcery to<br /> - Thaumaturgy<br /> - Dur An Ki<br /> - Akhu<br /> - Sadhana<br /> - Nahuallotl<br /> <br /> and Oblivion to<br /> - Obtenebration<br /> - Necromancy<br /> - Wanga<br /> <br /> is something that might need to be further explained into how can one possibly employ something that it couldn't do before. I personally hope the game the best, but I rather wait until I'm assured that some adaptations I worked for years in my chronicles might actually make a better sense that they do now.<br /> <br /> When Gehenna came out, the book considered Ventrue Antediluvian to be slain right after the Second City, which raised more flame than questions since the writers answers were &quot;errr.... he is beyond life and death&quot; which didn't made sense at all. An &quot;oops, we forgot about Mithras, Alexander and many more embrace dates&quot; would have been better instead of justifying with a lame improvised plot device (that is still being sustained!). Since this things happened before, I rather wait and see that V5 is above such carelessness.<br /> <br /> -Saga</div> </div> </div> </div>So. Plot devices, which are absolutely irrelevant to the game mechanics and can be represented as just that. But. Mithras can still command his entire blood line with a thought. For example: Ancestral Dominion is a Dominate 4, Blood Sorcery 3 amalgam that let's you dominate a descendant at any distance. It does admittedly not work if the vampire's defense pool goes above 10 but, Mithras might have a more powerful version of something like that. (That power is literally from the cult of Mithras) Mithras also at full strength would have BP 9 or 10. This means that even if he had a stamina of 1, he'd still have a health pool of 9. He could activate toughness for almost free, he can sling around Defy bane again, for almost free as well as Flesh of Marble. If he activated all of those powers, he'd have spent on average a whole 1 hunger.<br /> <br /> The Montano thing would be fitting for a ceremony given that Shadow Step is literally already a power, and so a Ceremony that extends it from &quot;Line of Sight&quot; to &quot;Anywhere in the world&quot; would fit within the power level and scope of the game.<br /> <br /> Ur-Shulgi and Al-Ashrad were... plot devices that weren't really represented in game anyways. In game terms, they'd have a minimum BP of 5 but more than likely have much more. Still, that BP of 5 means they get a minimum of 3 dice on every discipline, and can add three more at a whim. If they were max power, that goes up to 5 for the minimum and 5 for a surge. That means that they could have a pool of 20 with the barest of effort. Which in this system is pretty highly overkill<br /> <br /> Again, a plot point for the dragon thing. But something that would be doable as a max level power and or loresheet.<br /> <br /> Yes, a neonate can do these things. IF they know that it exists, IF they cultivate their blood that way, and IF they were to grow in that way.<br /> <br /> At the least, Thaumaturgy has always been represented as being able to do everything that everyone else can do. It's literally noted as being a highly flexible paradigm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24893-necroticbinder","name":"Necroticbinder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-11T12:30:24-07:00","id":1402277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Necroticbinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401610-how-do-you-express-elder-traits-disciplines-in-v5?p=1402256#post1402256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So. Plot devices, which are absolutely irrelevant to the game mechanics and can be represented as just that. But. Mithras can still command his entire blood line with a thought. For example: Ancestral Dominion is a Dominate 4, Blood Sorcery 3 amalgam that let's you dominate a descendant at any distance. It does admittedly not work if the vampire's defense pool goes above 10 but, Mithras might have a more powerful version of something like that. (That power is literally from the cult of Mithras) Mithras also at full strength would have BP 9 or 10. This means that even if he had a stamina of 1, he'd still have a health pool of 9. He could activate toughness for almost free, he can sling around Defy bane again, for almost free as well as Flesh of Marble. If he activated all of those powers, he'd have spent on average a whole 1 hunger.<br /> <br /> The Montano thing would be fitting for a ceremony given that Shadow Step is literally already a power, and so a Ceremony that extends it from &amp;quot;Line of Sight&amp;quot; to &amp;quot;Anywhere in the world&amp;quot; would fit within the power level and scope of the game.<br /> <br /> Ur-Shulgi and Al-Ashrad were... plot devices that weren't really represented in game anyways. In game terms, they'd have a minimum BP of 5 but more than likely have much more. Still, that BP of 5 means they get a minimum of 3 dice on every discipline, and can add three more at a whim. If they were max power, that goes up to 5 for the minimum and 5 for a surge. That means that they could have a pool of 20 with the barest of effort. Which in this system is pretty highly overkill<br /> <br /> Again, a plot point for the dragon thing. But something that would be doable as a max level power and or loresheet.<br /> <br /> Yes, a neonate can do these things. IF they know that it exists, IF they cultivate their blood that way, and IF they were to grow in that way.<br /> <br /> At the least, Thaumaturgy has always been represented as being able to do everything that everyone else can do. It's literally noted as being a highly flexible paradigm.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't compare to what Mihtras could do in VtM.<br /> <br /> In v5, an amalgam occupies a slot, that is, Mithras will have to sacrifice the power 4, Rationalize, to obtain that amalgam. An order given to 01 (one) descendant that would not be subtle, a victim would know that he/she was being dominated, restrict to a single victim, can last at most one turn or one scene... In addition to being able to simply fail against dicepool 10. <br /> <br /> In vtm, an command &quot;to work for the success of the Malkavian clan&quot; to the descendants is possible, including this example described in the described power. In v5, no. <br /> <br /> But why am I saying this, if we already know that vampires got weaker in v5? <br /> <br /> Because some fundamentals VtM things like making yourself Kupala, transforming into a Dragon, creating vozdh to get loose in New York, creating Gargoyles, were all part of the scenario and something that players can learn to do because the system was fear enough to apply the same rules to NPCs and PCs. Ring bells to NPCs in v5 whom don't have to follow Chronicle Tenants and even can be without Touchstones, like Talley. Fuck you, PCs! XD <br /> <br /> If my pj survived the chronicle contained in House Tremere having the opportunity to be initiated in the art of creating gargoyles, unlucky me, as it will not be viable in v5.<br /> <br /> From what you're describing to me, I either make this power disapear or handwave it as plot device. As an ST I would care less but as a player neither is satisfactory. The Elder can do it, because it's a plot device, but I can't and never will, no matter how much XP I have? Sir, this sucks. It seems that only ST can have fun in V5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-11T12:32:18-07:00","id":1402278,"title":"","content":"Here's a suggestion I posted a while ago:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1357567-v5-character-creation-houserules-for-ancillae-and-elders\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1357567-v5-character-creation-houserules-for-ancillae-and-elders\"> V5: character creation houserules for ancillae and elders - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1357567-v5-character-creation-houserules-for-ancillae-and-elders\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1357567-v5-character-creation-houserules-for-ancillae-and-elders </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Here's how I modified the character creation rules for elders and ancillae in V5. The idea is to show the diference in power between them and childer and neonates (neonates could be quite powerful in their own right though, depending on age). Let me know if you think they work or if/where you find them problematic and why please! Before starting character creation set a generation and age standard everyone should adhere. CHILDER: Embraced between the last 15 years. Basic character creation rules, no extra XP. NEONATE: Vampires with enough experience to start making their own way into the night, </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The problem for elders in V5 is not the lack of 6+ disciplines but the fact that for the moment the basic rules of character creation do not support them having POTENTIALLY more disciplines than a 13th gen fledgling. The moment you allow elders to have more than 5 powers for each discipline they posses they regain their advantage and amalgam disciplines duplicating old 6+ powers and creating new ones allow to make their arsenal more varied and effective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-11T13:04:34-07:00","id":1402280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blailton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401610-how-do-you-express-elder-traits-disciplines-in-v5?p=1402277#post1402277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what you're describing to me, I either make this power disapear or handwave it as plot device. As an ST I would care less but as a player neither is satisfactory. The Elder can do it, because it's a plot device, but I can't and never will, no matter how much XP I have? Sir, this sucks. It seems that only ST can have fun in V5.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean\u2026as I said before, how often have you actually used level-nine disciplines as a player? And the Gehenna book literally replaced all level-ten disciplines with &quot;Plot Device&quot;, those exact words.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-11T13:10:06-07:00","id":1402282,"title":"","content":"But you see, you only get one point of xp each session, so an elder having 5 in a discipline is really impressive now \u2e2e<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Actually, I should speak as a player, that this is something I have done several times already and it's quite fun. </div> </div> </div>Were your players all Gangrel or something?<br /> <br /> It's a change that effects some clans a lot more than others. I might not be that affected as a gangrel, but I sure as hell would be upset as a Tremere, Malkavian or Lasombra. Animalism, Presence , Fortitude and Protean are pretty close to what they were and you could perhaps have fun with some new features replacing stuff you didn't use, and I suppose you could look at Celerity's changes and think 'that's fair', But Auspex, Dominate, Obfuscate, Potence plus the rarer disciplines of Oblivion and Sorcery change the characters to utterly different entities; The things I did with 3 in Auspex, Dominate and Obfuscate (Impersonate a person, Use his persona to get close to his associates in order to dominate them for information and cause chaos, and use a load of auspex tricks on the way to help this go smoothly) I cannot do in V5. I'd also have to completely rethink my strategy with using potence because It isn't universal strength now and all the extra damage in the world won't help me if I can't get a hit in (A 2 strength, 2 brawl, 4 potence character went from amazing to useless), and I don't think I need to explain the deal with sorcery and oblivion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-11T14:03:25-07:00","id":1402288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401610-how-do-you-express-elder-traits-disciplines-in-v5?p=1402282#post1402282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But you see, you only get one point of xp each session, so an elder having 5 in a discipline is really impressive now \u2e2e<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well in V5 when you commit diablerie you gain 5xp you can spend on blood potency OR disciplines known to the victim for each success on the contested roll to subsume the diablerized vampire's heartblood. If you roll 5 successes you gain 25XP, which is a lot considering the 1 XP per session rule...<br /> <br /> Considering how you keep insisting on diablerie as means of increasing the power of PCs (what diablerie means doesn't seem to bother you much onestly... it's power after all!) seems to me you should be happy for V5 diablerie rules. Potentially they make diablerie much miore effective than it ever was making diablerist stronger.<br /> <br /> P.S.<br /> <br /> In all seriousness I think we can all agree that as the game progresses and PCs get more stuff to spend XP on increasing XP gain becomes a no brainer and by the way it's something I'm pretty sure already happens in famous chronicles like LA by night where players got several disciplines powers that would have been impossible to get if the 1XP per session rule were implemented.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-11T14:27:06-07:00","id":1402293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401610-how-do-you-express-elder-traits-disciplines-in-v5?p=1402280#post1402280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean\u2026as I said before, how often have you actually used level-nine disciplines as a player? And the Gehenna book literally replaced all level-ten disciplines with &amp;quot;Plot Device&amp;quot;, those exact words.</div> </div> </div> </div>Create gorg, vozdh, turn dragon, became Kupala are not level 10 or 9 or 8 or 7 power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-11T14:32:19-07:00","id":1402295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401610-how-do-you-express-elder-traits-disciplines-in-v5?p=1402288#post1402288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well in V5 when you commit diablerie you gain 5xp you can spend on blood potency OR disciplines known to the victim for each success on the contested roll to subsume the diablerized vampire's heartblood. If you roll 5 successes you gain 25XP, which is a lot considering the 1 XP per session rule...<br /> <br /> Considering how you keep insisting on diablerie as means of increasing the power of PCs (what diablerie means doesn't seem to bother you much onestly... it's power after all!) seems to me you should be happy for V5 diablerie rules. Potentially they make diablerie much miore effective than it ever was making diablerist stronger.<br /> <br /> P.S.<br /> <br /> In all seriousness I think we can all agree that as the game progresses and PCs get more stuff to spend XP on increasing XP gain becomes a no brainer and by the way it's something I'm pretty sure already happens in famous chronicles like LA by night where players got several disciplines powers that would have been impossible to get if the 1XP per session rule were implemented.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I call that as a Homebrew. Mason used his ST powers to implement golden rules into his game. I will not adopt his gold rules, however. And as a player I don't have evidence in the corebook to proof to the ST he/she should give me X points of xp instead of Y.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-11T15:34:18-07:00","id":1402310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401610-how-do-you-express-elder-traits-disciplines-in-v5?p=1402288#post1402288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stuff</div> </div> </div> </div>You know I've also posted that I also really don't like giving buckets of XP to Diablerists? For me, Diablerie should be little lost, little gained.<br /> I mean, I've played games where I've been given lots of disciplines from diablerie, and that's all very exciting when it goes to your head, But when your Physical-Tertiary mastermind can now out-brute the other players' brutes thanks to a windfall, the party dynamic suffers a bit. &quot;UNLIMITED POOOWWWWER&quot; is best when it's time limited. The V5 system for diablerie Is also hilariously the worst of a lot of worlds in that you gain far too much power if you eat with high humanity but don't make any gains if you devour someone while you have low humanity; So you should fear the saints, not the sinners.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now, for XP<br /> I'm genuinely considering that the 1xp per session thing works under the assumption that you are supposed to farm resonances to make up for the lackluster amount of XP. The primary goal of the Coterie (other than to survive) is to find (or create) individuals with strong resonances, as those people can grant XP for specific disciplines. You add them to your herd, feed off them with some regularity, and find more people so you can do this for a good amount. Sustainably, the right person could give you 1xp per six to eight weeks (assuming you're not encouraging them to really replenish those RBCs, and this is also assuming that the victim's resonance doesn't change) So if you found enough of these people and kept tabs on them and other vampires don't poach from you, you could get some pretty good results during downtime (The biggest problem, however, is that you're part of a coterie, so 'dibs' doesn't really work all that well)<br /> <br /> Assuming 6 week recovery times and an in-clan discipline (V5 is 5x level wanted, right?) your first dot of a discipline is 30 weeks (or 42 for an OOC) of feeding from one person every six weeks. If you find a second person with the same resonance, that's 15, and then it's 7. It's far more likely you'll find people of different resonances, but even then you're not making small gains assuming the storyteller gives you ample downtime. (We're also assuming you're spending your 1xp per session on Attributes and abilities, for some reason...)<br /> <br /> But then again I don't know how common resonances are supposed to be, if red blood cells are really relevant, if your storyteller will keep blood benefits consistent...<br /> <br /> But, assuming all things are correct, and you have target one person with a resonance granting xp for your in clan discipline once every six weeks, it should take you 8.6 Years for a level 5 discipline. (Wow that's shockingly short, though this is an optimistic projection)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-11T16:20:17-07:00","id":1402319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blailton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401610-how-do-you-express-elder-traits-disciplines-in-v5?p=1402293#post1402293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Create gorg, vozdh, turn dragon, became Kupala are not level 10 or 9 or 8 or 7 power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right; I don't relegate &quot;create vozhd&quot; to Plot Device tier, I would call that a Project requiring a bunch of Vicissitude (but not anything above level 5). I don't remember the &quot;become Kupala&quot; power but I would assume that <i>is</i> Plot Device tier because Kupala is, iirc, a tremendously powerful Earthbound.<br /> <br /> Most Plot Device tier things are the ones player characters will never get or use, like the level-nine Obeah that raises someone from the dead but permanently lowers your Path rating (which cannot then be raised by any means). That seems clearly designed as a plot device for NPC Salubri, not for player use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-11T21:03:52-07:00","id":1402358,"title":"","content":"I guess create Vozhd could be an amalgam with Vicissitude (or Protean if they decide to go that route with it) and Animalism. Another possibility is a Koldunic ritual that needs at least a few dots in Vicissitude/Protean with the right powers picked in the discipline that make sense to do that. That would depend on how they handle Koldunism, like is it just a different set of powers in Blood Sorcery or it's own thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14519-drhappyangry","name":"DrHappyAngry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14519_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-11T22:03:08-07:00","id":1402368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401610-how-do-you-express-elder-traits-disciplines-in-v5?p=1402280#post1402280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean\u2026as I said before, how often have you actually used level-nine disciplines as a player? And the Gehenna book literally replaced all level-ten disciplines with &quot;Plot Device&quot;, those exact words.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing with level 9 powers is that the ST can use it and as a player you know what is he really using (not in character obviously) and that usually create more awe in the PCs than an invented plot device could.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1594,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","user":"Saga","date":". 07-12-2020, 01:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-11T22:11:58-07:00","id":1402369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blailton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401610-how-do-you-express-elder-traits-disciplines-in-v5?p=1402293#post1402293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Create gorg, vozdh, turn dragon, became Kupala are not level 10 or 9 or 8 or 7 power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually to turn into dragon form it was a Vicissitude 9 in VtDA20 and Vicissitude 9 (+Koldunic 9) in the original VtDA (Libellus Sanguinis I)<br /> <br /> Another one was mythic form with Protean 8 (Clanbook Gangrel revised)<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-12T04:56:13-07:00","id":1402395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401610-how-do-you-express-elder-traits-disciplines-in-v5?p=1402369#post1402369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually to turn into dragon form it was a Vicissitude 9 in VtDA20 and Vicissitude 9 (+Koldunic 9) in the original VtDA (Libellus Sanguinis I)<br /> <br /> Another one was mythic form with Protean 8 (Clanbook Gangrel revised)<br /> <br /> - Saga</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes I was reffering to the Protean one. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-13T19:47:08-07:00","id":1402716,"title":"","content":"I can see all the &quot;turn into a giant legendary beast&quot; powers being amalgams of Protean 4 and Animalism 4 or 5. Which are probably well within the reach of Gangrel and Tzimisce elders if they want to develop their powers in that direction, and would still involve about as many discipline dots as before, just spread across multiple disciplines.<br /> <br /> I think the big wide scale feats of sorcery like laying (and breaking) curses on an entire bloodline or clan are probably best done as projects. Back in the days of Revised I didn't think a discrete high-level ritual or power that would only ever have a single appropriate use was the best way to emulate things that were described in fluff as years or centuries of experimentation and cooperation among multiple sorcerers. Likewise for creating vozhd, gargoyles, setting up magically protected castles in the Carpathians, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-14T03:39:36-07:00","id":1402775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401610-how-do-you-express-elder-traits-disciplines-in-v5?p=1402716#post1402716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can see all the &amp;quot;turn into a giant legendary beast&amp;quot; powers being amalgams of Protean 4 and Animalism 4 or 5. <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>And Apep for Setites?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-14T17:13:04-07:00","id":1402884,"title":"","content":"Sure. Perhaps not as natural a fit for the Ministry as the two clans above, but if one's determined to go the Thulsa Doom route they'd be able to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-05T08:21:05-07:00","id":1406444,"title":"","content":"I'm thinking 5e wanted to tone down the power levels, which makes sense given how cray cray many elders were in previous editions. Though note that generation and blood potency still matters a great deal in this edition, and elders with 6+ BP and a bunch of rank 5 disciples could still mangle a coterie of neonates. Though with less of an obvious power difference, it finally highlights something that really should have been apparent in earlier editions: elders survive by being smart, not strong. Lots of advance planning, safeguards, and blood bound bodyguards. A 200 scheming Ventrue is going to be much more of a threat than a rampaging idiot twice his age.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2462-karlb","name":"KarlB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-09T23:15:05-07:00","id":1407239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401610-how-do-you-express-elder-traits-disciplines-in-v5?p=1402280#post1402280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean\u2026as I said before, how often have you actually used level-nine disciplines as a player? And the Gehenna book literally replaced all level-ten disciplines with &quot;Plot Device&quot;, those exact words.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that was controversial to a lot of plays considering that level 10 disciplines were stated out in first and second edition. They weren't godly or over-powered either, they were straight-forward things like quietus 10 letting a vampire blood-bond bond others using a single drink of their blood instead of 3.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KarlB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401610-how-do-you-express-elder-traits-disciplines-in-v5?p=1406444#post1406444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm thinking 5e wanted to tone down the power levels, which makes sense given how cray cray many elders were in previous editions. Though note that generation and blood potency still matters a great deal in this edition, and elders with 6+ BP and a bunch of rank 5 disciples could still mangle a coterie of neonates. Though with less of an obvious power difference, it finally highlights something that really should have been apparent in earlier editions: elders survive by being smart, not strong. Lots of advance planning, safeguards, and blood bound bodyguards. A 200 scheming Ventrue is going to be much more of a threat than a rampaging idiot twice his age.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem with trimming back power levels is that it limits the available types of gameplay. V20 and previous editions allowed for stories to be what I'll call &quot;epic horror&quot;, grand adventures like the illiad/odyssey with a distinctly horror bend. The &quot;power level&quot; were important for giving a sense of scale to these games, and those same type of games are shallower without it.<br /> <br /> I'll just say what I've been saying for a while. I get that personal horror is an important element to VTM and liked how it was used before, but I feel V5 wants to make it the Only element and I don't like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T09:30:29-07:00","id":1407313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KarlB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401610-how-do-you-express-elder-traits-disciplines-in-v5?p=1406444#post1406444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> elders survive by being smart, not strong. Lots of advance planning, safeguards, and blood bound bodyguards.</div> </div> </div> </div>You say that, but much of the confirmable V5 metaplot hinges on the idea that elders aren't that smart.<br /> <br /> <br /> The thing is, Neonates can be really, really smart. Not many players play them that smart, but you don't need 3 intellegence or wits for planning and safeguards. A lot of neonates were chosen because their sires thought they could cut it, and that tends to imply some base competence (rarely found in most first time players) You just need a short amount of time to really think things through. I virtually never set my mentals as Tertiary; it's better to be weak or unsocial than an idiot, and the characters I DO play as idiots are typically characters dependent on others, and characters who are dependent on the right others can also last a long time.<br /> <br /> But also, a character who is just smart... is still kinda easy to off?<br /> <br /> The terrors of elders comes from their profound peresonal strength that takes centuries to accumulate. I can make a starting character with 4 intelegence, have him make bombs, give him a flawless delivery method, and take out any other clever elder character... That is unless they can shrug off those bombs, or sense them before they become a threat, or I can't possibly find where that elder rests or what car his people drive or.... and then that elder might have the means to trace those bombs back to me. Hell the elder could be on me before I even manufacture the damn things.<br /> <br /> Toning down the power levels means I no longer live in fear of the prince; I'm pretty sure I can take him out and get away with it if I really set myself to it. But you give elders the power and oh boy, they become difficult. I might still be able to kill difficult, but it's a lot harder to avoid fallout when trying to bomb <i>difficult and his many difficult friends. </i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T10:08:57-07:00","id":1407320,"title":"","content":"Note that Elders will still have considerably stronger vampiric powers than a fledgling neonate. Sure, they don't have 6+ dots in anything, but having a much better blood potency and a bunch of level 4+ disciplines can still crush said neonate without breaking a sweat. But do remember that powerful vampire elders were in a massive panic during the late middle ages when many young vampires kicked off the Anarch Revolt by killing off elders. In the end, the elders managed to contain it, but not without the loss of a considerable number of them. A half dozen angry neonates could easily take down a powerful elder if they are prepared.<br /> <br /> Now as for smart vs not smart ... the basic premise of V5 is that elders, while very experienced and powerful, really struggle with the rapid advancements of technology and global communication. But other than that, elders survived because they have learned from centuries of experience how to counter younger kindred by being one step ahead of them. Neonates adapt much better to changing technology and social standards, but can't hold a candle to the wind when it comes to politics, surveillance, currying favors, and making sure that any potential rivals do not gain an advantage on them. So in the case of your bomb maker, said elder knows what bombs are, knows or knows someone who knows how to get necessary supplies on the black market, and will have contacts in the police to set up surveillance on someone they suspect of being a possible threat. Not saying it's not possible for that bomb maker kindred to get away with it, but they would need to execute their plan impeccably and in absolute secrecy. If I'm GMing and a player REALLY does their research and plans things meticulously, I'd certainly allow them to get a shot at that elder. But if they act impulsively, I'd likely rule that said elder is aware something is amiss and has started actively seeking out your neonate's weaknesses with plans to destroy them if they pose a threat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2462-karlb","name":"KarlB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T11:06:55-07:00","id":1407331,"title":"","content":"Not really. more powers in V5 are weaker than not, and blood potency granting extra dice is weaker than allowing traits higher than 5. There are no powers in V5 that crush an unexpected bomb attack, and all the potence in the world doesn't work if you can't land a hit on someone. <br /> <br /> (also, your player just needs his character to have the knowledge on how to do these things, with the right dice collected. They themselves don't need to end up on a watch list. That said, I'm given to understand that powerful IEDs can be made from commercially available products that aren't really monitored.) <br /> <br /> Elders being incapable of using technology has always been half-writer's lack of knowledge and another half writers fiat; In the absolute worst case they have retainers who can do the tech things for them and explain the basic principles of such things. An elder doesn't need to know how cameras work, only that they exist, and cameras in some form have been around for a <i>long</i> time (1825) but I'm willing to gander the average, jaded elder would put far more interest into modern novelties than many would give them credit for. In any case, the SI issue isn't primarily a problem of technology, it's a problem of politics; the elders apparently put half baked tentacles into things they don't understand, which are really hard to get into in the first place if you don't understand them, and fucked up monumentally with no backup plans... as you said, elders should be really good when it comes to politics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-11T19:05:12-07:00","id":1407644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401610-how-do-you-express-elder-traits-disciplines-in-v5#post1401610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">AFAIK there is no 6+ traits in V5 now and many people have scoffed at this. So how will you express them of older editions in V5?<br /> <br /> My brief thoughts:<br /> 1. Traits: Just like what they had done (Blood Potency, etc.) and Werewolf, raise some new traits and you can add them in your dice pool. Ancestor, Past Life, Renown and so on<br /> <br /> 2. Disciplines:<br /> All level 5-9 disciplines of older editions are folded into the single level 5 and appropriate combo ones, but they are still required something effective (Generation or whatever) to learn, exp you spend depends on the strength, for example (I haven't converted the system):<br /> <br /> Of course for me I will modify overpowerful disciplines, making them more reasonable<br /> <br /> Tip:<br /> 1. I will also fold all forms of blood magic(Dur-An-Ki, Koldun, Thaumaturgy, etc.) into the single Blood Sorcery and just leave some options to different ones, making they have more differences in culture or region rather than actual changes<br /> 2. To some Clan or Bloodline Disciplines, I will refine them, making they have more differences in style rather than actual change. For example, I give make Tzimisce Protean, not Vissicitude, but this kind of Protean will appear more &quot;flesh&quot; and &quot;horrible&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair they aren't all folded into level 5's, several Elder Powers are lower then 5 but without the initial option of multiple options for each level they just shunted them to 6+ where you do have the option for multiple variants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-12T04:31:13-07:00","id":1407673,"title":"","content":"By ignoring V5 rules<br /> <br /> V5 vampires are nerfed to street level monster and no matter how powerful or old you get by RAW rules a goon can just buy a raufoss and deal agg +5 (more damage that any amalgam or Discipline at max does) with his dex stat from a distance you cannot counter.<br /> <br /> People want to play V5 like V20 and don\u00b4t realize it is a different game with different mechanics and a completely different setting becuase many things changed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-12T07:54:35-07:00","id":1407696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leandro16</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401610-how-do-you-express-elder-traits-disciplines-in-v5?p=1407673#post1407673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By ignoring V5 rules<br /> <br /> V5 vampires are nerfed to street level monster and no matter how powerful or old you get by RAW rules a goon can just buy a raufoss and deal agg +5 (more damage that any amalgam or Discipline at max does) with his dex stat from a distance you cannot counter.<br /> <br /> People want to play V5 like V20 and don\u00b4t realize it is a different game with different mechanics and a completely different setting becuase many things changed.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Exactly. I think Paradox/Modiphius are trying their best to cut back dramatically on the *massive* power creep that was Revised and V20. Trying to make the game more personal in scope rather than making everything godlike and epic which was a huge problem for oWOD back in the late 90s and ended up killing the line in favor of the, you guessed it, more personal horror side of VTR. I think this is a really good move on their part. Especially since we know there likely WILL be some power creep even in V5, but at least the baseline now is much lower.<br /> <br /> Notable example: Helena from Chicago by Night went from having 44 points worth of disciplines to 'just' 29. She's still crazy freaking strong, but now it's actually possible to take her down with enough planning and effort. Unlike her Auspex 7 and Dominate 8 of old that basically gave her the kind of power to sense and control hundreds if not thousands at a whim.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2462-karlb","name":"KarlB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-12T09:29:46-07:00","id":1407714,"title":"","content":"With the exception of V20, did we see 6+ disciplines in the core book before? I don't recall them being in there, as they were included in further supplements that focused on Elders and such. Dark Ages could be a notable exception, as at character generation, a character could be 7th generation, and there by eventually learn level 6 powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24641-sarcasticjazzhands","name":"SarcasticJazzHands","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-12T11:05:26-07:00","id":1407728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KarlB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401610-how-do-you-express-elder-traits-disciplines-in-v5?p=1407696#post1407696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Exactly. I think Paradox/Modiphius are trying their best to cut back dramatically on the *massive* power creep that was Revised and V20. Trying to make the game more personal in scope rather than making everything godlike and epic which was a huge problem for oWOD back in the late 90s and ended up killing the line in favor of the, you guessed it, more personal horror side of VTR. I think this is a really good move on their part. Especially since we know there likely WILL be some power creep even in V5, but at least the baseline now is much lower.<br /> <br /> Notable example: Helena from Chicago by Night went from having 44 points worth of disciplines to 'just' 29. She's still crazy freaking strong, but now it's actually possible to take her down with enough planning and effort. Unlike her Auspex 7 and Dominate 8 of old that basically gave her the kind of power to sense and control hundreds if not thousands at a whim.</div> </div> </div> </div>If they wanted a VtR style game why make it an edition of VtM? Serious question, the demigods at the top of the Jyhad was a core theme of VtM from the start, and now the rules simply do not support them, at all, that sense of impending doom they bought is gone...and of the answer is houserule it, why bother buying anything for the system? VtR already covers the game style that VtM now seems to be forcing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-12T12:07:09-07:00","id":1407743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401610-how-do-you-express-elder-traits-disciplines-in-v5?p=1407728#post1407728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If they wanted a VtR style game why make it an edition of VtM? Serious question, the demigods at the top of the Jyhad was a core theme of VtM from the start, and now the rules simply do not support them, at all, that sense of impending doom they bought is gone...and of the answer is houserule it, why bother buying anything for the system? VtR already covers the game style that VtM now seems to be forcing.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Simple: Because powercreep is a big problem and tends to lead to the downfall of gaming lines. PCs like to feel like they might have an impact, and if they know that an NPC has a power level FAR FAR above anything they could ever hope to accomplish or even counter through numbers, it just leads to jaded players. By toning down the power levels across the board, the players feel like they might have a chance without resorting to finding the most broken and imbalanced content to play with. For example that horrible horrible mess that was Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand.<br /> <br /> Though note one important thing, though: Level 5 powers in V5 are noticeably stronger than they used to be, more in line with level 6 or 7 powers of old. I mean, in the current edition, Helena is more than capable of telling a PC to shoot himself in the head ... and he'll do it as he can't possibly hope to counter her incredible 13 dice pool (5 Manipulation+5 Dominate+3 bonus dice from blood potency) when issuing said terminal command. Or maybe she could instead command the entire party at the same time to lie down on the ground and shut up. Or she could, you know, turn on Majesty and turn them all into gibbering sycophants.<br /> <br /> It's presumptuous to assume that methusalehs are weak in any way, shape, or form in this edition. They just changed how discipline and discipline rolls work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2462-karlb","name":"KarlB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-12T12:39:57-07:00","id":1407754,"title":"","content":"Karl, you seem to be the apotheosis of the idea that &quot;the player doesn't know what's good for them&quot; <br /> Designers need to give characters a challenge. The leveled playing field of V5 does not give players a challenge. The seemingly insurmountable power of elders in prior editions gives players a challenge, and the daunting prospect of fighting absolute monsters adds to the horror of the setting. Players having a noticable impact due to the low power gap also poses problems in that there's not actually much to do; If they can topple the prince and his puppet master in a couple of sessions, what else is there to do? <br /> <br /> Now sure, you could argue that 5th level powers are stronger, but 1,2,3 and 4 are generally weaker. But the thing is, general use wise you're using low level powers. High leveled powers are niche. This is and continues to be true for methuselah and V5. The ancient might have potence 5, but he has to hit me first. The prince might be indistructible to one attack each turn, but there are three of us and we've got a surprise round... Helena might be more capable of getting the player to shoot themselves, but she's no longer capable at orchestrating covert Dominate puppeteer masterplans from a safe distance to the degree she once did (no, she doesn't need 8 Dominate for that, but she has 8 Dominate); and that's really what elders and ancients should be doing with Dominate; Terminal decree is a power for hacks who can't scheme.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-12T12:56:18-07:00","id":1407756,"title":"","content":"But think about what you just wrote, though. Having a super scary Dominate power that can mass affect people that aren't even at the same location as her makes going up against her a totally lost cause. She feels threatened? Boom ... Dominate *everyone* in the district. Problem solved for her. Horrible problem for the PCs. I get that it's important for PCs to be terrified of such a formidable foe. But telling PCs that they are trying to counter an NPC so powerful that she's less antagonist and more an insurmountable plot point just ends up with annoyed players. No one likes being railroaded like that. And that's what Methuselahs of old used to be: literal gods GMs could use to turn the story any way they felt like without players being able to do a damn thing about it. By toning down the power levels across the board (note that PCs are also weaker on average than before), it flattens that curve and makes PC objectives actually attainable. Still *extremely* challenging, but it is attainable. It's also why The Beckoning is a thing ... it removes the most powerful NPCs from the local area and allows PC actions to *matter*. They can play a political game without worrying that the 5th generation thousand year old Prince of the city won't just instantly kill them all within seconds just on a whim.<br /> <br /> Now if you are of the opinion that PCs *should* face situations they cannot possibly have *any* control over because the antagonists are walking gods, then fine, stick with Revised/V20. Different strokes for different folks and all that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2462-karlb","name":"KarlB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-12T13:32:48-07:00","id":1407762,"title":"","content":"No such power exists, but I digress: When you're good at a game, do you prefer playing on hard or easy? (and I'm not talking about novelty -extreme- difficulties ) <br /> Methuselahs, generally, won't bother with small fry players unless they screw up really, really badly. They're generally not a monster you're fighting tooth and nail with until you actually become capable of dealing with them and act against them. Players have the agency to<i> choose their battles</i>. Vampire might involve a lot of kicking ass and taking names, but it's not about that, the central conflict is about the struggle, the Jyhad. Players are to look for smaller victories to prep them for the big ones, or to avoid loss. Vampire isn't about winning, you win when you slay god, and that's a far off goal. Vampire is about <i>not losing, </i>and clinging on with everything you got to make your unlife comfortable and achieve some small personal goals in the face of a storm. If you aren't ready to face Helena, don't piss her off, don't give her a reason to come down on you personally; Short of a linear campaign that's how you're supposed to play, how you're supposed to live your unlife. Methuselah's aren't a challenge that needs to be overcome, they're a <i>potential</i> challenge. You're supposed to navigate the web of undead living with some semblance of intelligence; V5 dumbing that down by leveling the playing field is not a good thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-12T22:51:11-07:00","id":1407868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KarlB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401610-how-do-you-express-elder-traits-disciplines-in-v5?p=1407743#post1407743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Simple: Because powercreep is a big problem and tends to lead to the downfall of gaming lines. PCs like to feel like they might have an impact, and if they know that an NPC has a power level FAR FAR above anything they could ever hope to accomplish or even counter through numbers, it just leads to jaded players. By toning down the power levels across the board, the players feel like they might have a chance without resorting to finding the most broken and imbalanced content to play with. For example that horrible horrible mess that was Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand.<br /> <br /> Though note one important thing, though: Level 5 powers in V5 are noticeably stronger than they used to be, more in line with level 6 or 7 powers of old. I mean, in the current edition, Helena is more than capable of telling a PC to shoot himself in the head ... and he'll do it as he can't possibly hope to counter her incredible 13 dice pool (5 Manipulation+5 Dominate+3 bonus dice from blood potency) when issuing said terminal command. Or maybe she could instead command the entire party at the same time to lie down on the ground and shut up. Or she could, you know, turn on Majesty and turn them all into gibbering sycophants.<br /> <br /> It's presumptuous to assume that methusalehs are weak in any way, shape, or form in this edition. They just changed how discipline and discipline rolls work.</div> </div> </div> </div>That describes elders, Methuselahs should be continent level threats that is what they are for, when gods walk characters flee, that is the horror of them, that knowledge that you can never win, no matter what you do, it is all for nought if the ancients notice you. The Prince and Primogen you might kill, with extreme planning, but their masters are beyond you,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 08-13-2020, 01:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T02:39:29-07:00","id":1407879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KarlB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401610-how-do-you-express-elder-traits-disciplines-in-v5?p=1407696#post1407696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Exactly. I think Paradox/Modiphius are trying their best to cut back dramatically on the *massive* power creep that was Revised and V20. Trying to make the game more personal in scope rather than making everything godlike and epic which was a huge problem for oWOD back in the late 90s and ended up killing the line in favor of the, you guessed it, more personal horror side of VTR. I think this is a really good move on their part. Especially since we know there likely WILL be some power creep even in V5, but at least the baseline now is much lower.</div> </div> </div> </div> VTR is a toolbox edition designated to be played on multiple tiers (street level , city level and global conspiracy) and has crazier stuff than masquerade antedeluvians from the gehena it is the opposite of V5.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KarlB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401610-how-do-you-express-elder-traits-disciplines-in-v5?p=1407696#post1407696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Notable example: Helena from Chicago by Night went from having 44 points worth of disciplines to 'just' 29. She's still crazy freaking strong, but now it's actually possible to take her down with enough planning and effort. Unlike her Auspex 7 and Dominate 8 of old that basically gave her the kind of power to sense and control hundreds if not thousands at a whim.</div> </div> </div> </div>3 dices is the difference between Horatio Ballard and Helena Dominate... A coterie of starting characters from the clan Nosferatu can fairly easily destroy Helena and even a goon with a lucky shot can so just add more goons and helena bites the dust.<br /> <br /> The problem of V5 wasnt tonning down the power levels it was eliminating them and triying to kept &quot;the masquerade&quot; in the tittle to get more sales and this generated a backlash from the comunnity.<br /> <br /> Ironically V5 could have worked as a different gameline or as a supplement with alternate rules for V20","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":24037,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","user":"Leandro16","date":". 08-13-2020, 05:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T05:17:44-07:00","id":1407898,"title":"","content":"I found myself trying to figure out how to port over Elder Vampires from OWoD to a V5 setting, which when I had the original character sheets provided in media was a help (and also helped me explain to players who have played OWoD but not V5 what has changed better) I found myself at a loss at what to do concerning higher level powers as well as just combining similar skills to give higher dice pools and more specialties.<br /> <br /> I found myself thinking of a good way to balance it was to limit XP players get to make sure they aren't creeping to the level of my Elder NPCs. And I think it's working. Plus, you can still instill fear in characters without rolling dice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Storyteller of Boston by Night on Twitch <a href=\"https://www.twitch.tv/theonyxpath\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.twitch.tv/theonyxpath</a><br /> Fan of WOD Since 2013","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26354-michelleclight","name":"MichelleCLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26354_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T07:54:20-07:00","id":1407938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leandro16</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401610-how-do-you-express-elder-traits-disciplines-in-v5?p=1407879#post1407879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> VTR is a toolbox edition designated to be played on multiple tiers (street level , city level and global conspiracy) and has crazier stuff than masquerade antedeluvians from the gehena it is the opposite of V5.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 3 dices is the difference between Horatio Ballard and Helena Dominate... A coterie of starting characters from the clan Nosferatu can fairly easily destroy Helena and even a goon with a lucky shot can so just add more goons and helena bites the dust.<br /> <br /> The problem of V5 wasnt tonning down the power levels it was eliminating them and triying to kept &quot;the masquerade&quot; in the tittle to get more sales and this generated a backlash from the comunnity.<br /> <br /> Ironically V5 could have worked as a different gameline or as a supplement with alternate rules for V20</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Please note that ancient vampires in V5 and V20 both roll roughly the same number of dice when using disciplines. It's just that in V20, these characters had 6+ dots in both attribute and discipline, whereas in V5, they are capped at five each ... but then add another bonus based on blood potency. So in reality, the only real difference is they don't have these crazy 6+ dot discipline powers, but on the other hand, 5 dot powers in V5 are overall stronger than 5 dot powers of old ... without drifting into GM plot territory by having game changing and railroading powers at their disposal. Player characters themselves pretty much never had access to these insane powers as PCs were generally capped at 8th gen and it's 5 dot limit. So in the end, all these powers served was to show players what they *could* have if they were themselves these powerful ancients ... or, as was pretty much ALWAYS the case in old editions, the ability to start chargen at 8th gen and then find excuses to diablerize.<br /> <br /> Note: Helena is by no means weak in the new edition. Not even close. She still has a bunch of 5 dot disciplines as well as many 5 dot attributes and abilities. Not to mention a high enough blood potency so that she gets an automatic 3 dice added to every discipline roll. And as I said, level 5 disciplines now are really powerful given they are meant to be capstones. For example, Majesty doesn't break against everyone if the majestic vampire attacks a goon. In fact, even the goon attacked is still only defending himself ... but would still struggle to attack her back. And combine that with, say, Terminal Decree, and you could have several dozen goons that are all cowed by her, unable to do anything but grovel, and watch helplessly as their leader goes blank eyed, aims his gun at his own temple, and pulls the trigger. Trust me, she's still quite badass. Without drifting into GM railroading territory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2462-karlb","name":"KarlB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T07:55:55-07:00","id":1407940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MichelleCLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401610-how-do-you-express-elder-traits-disciplines-in-v5?p=1407898#post1407898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I found myself trying to figure out how to port over Elder Vampires from OWoD to a V5 setting, which when I had the original character sheets provided in media was a help (and also helped me explain to players who have played OWoD but not V5 what has changed better) I found myself at a loss at what to do concerning higher level powers as well as just combining similar skills to give higher dice pools and more specialties.<br /> <br /> I found myself thinking of a good way to balance it was to limit XP players get to make sure they aren't creeping to the level of my Elder NPCs. And I think it's working. Plus, you can still instill fear in characters without rolling dice.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's actually the case RAW. XP gain is a bit lower than previous editions, and XP costs are noticeably higher. It takes a lot longer for PCs to reach elder like powers now. So overall, power levels are lower across the board.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2462-karlb","name":"KarlB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T08:48:11-07:00","id":1407954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KarlB</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Simple: Because powercreep is a big problem and tends to lead to the downfall of gaming lines. PCs like to feel like they might have an impact, and if they know that an NPC has a power level FAR FAR above anything they could ever hope to accomplish or even counter through numbers, it just leads to jaded players. By toning down the power levels across the board, the players feel like they might have a chance without resorting to finding the most broken and imbalanced content to play with. For example that horrible horrible mess that was Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't believe this premise is true. And your example it's the perfect proof: Old DSotBH actually allowed you to start the game with a Meth or close (their had an &quot;special&quot; Generation Background), that's also an assasin of a secret society with True Magick and Werewolf-vampires among their resources - so it was the least de-powering sourcebook of all of Vampire that I know. It still was a disaster.<br /> <br /> On the other hand D&amp;D 5e (a game that's very well liked among fans both old and new) has monsters with CR above 20. That's above what characters of max level can figth comfortably. And what lvl 20 characters can figth it's already WAY beyond anything lvl 1 starting characters can ever hope to defeat with their resources<br /> <br /> As evidence shows, this doesn't <i>need </i>to lead to 'jaded players'. Poor storytelling shoving high-end treaths to low tier groups, that both by common sense and Lore should be beneath their notice, it's what leads to jaded players.<br /> <br /> And I will admit that my experience with Vampire has seen many of these. I guess, it's possible V5 it's a (too little, WAY too late) reaction to the tendency of STs of days of yore to shove Meths against the players to <s>control and abuse</s> to create horror ... but this can't really be attributed to mere rules. This kind of antagonistic storytelling was encouraged by books - <i>and it still kinda is</i>, albeit in a different fashion (just see how V5 suggest STs &quot;worth their salt&quot; to treat PC Touchstones).<br /> <br /> You need a <i>narration</i> that's not about punishing your players (except when they like it :P ) to avoid this. After all, as has been said, Helena can easily break the PC if the ST wishes to force such a confrontation when they aren't capable of figthing her. I don't think that was ever <i>the problem</i>, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MichelleCLight</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I found myself thinking of a good way to balance it was to limit XP players get to make sure they aren't creeping to the level of my Elder NPCs. And I think it's working.</div> </div> </div> </div>You give the players <i>less </i>than the 1-2 xp per session that V5 grant's them <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <hr /><br /> Personally, I think that the problem it's not so much that powers can't get over 5, but rather that<br /> <br /> 1\u00b0 Elders (and anyone, really) <i>can only ever get 5 powers</i>.<br /> 2\u00b0 This isn't tied to generation or anything inherently &quot;elderly&quot;, but to XP - and this can't really be solved by making the XP gain even more abysmal for reasons I will mention below.<br /> <br /> As mentioned level 5 disciplines can duplicate some Elder powers. Problem is you can't ever have more than 5 powers in a Discipline (less than that if you use Amalgams). Helena has to <i>choose </i>between being able to order a single PC to shoot himself OR being able to dominate all of the PC OR have some other single high-tier gimmick (and once you see it, you know that she hasn't the other powers. Understanding the enemy skills it's the 1rst step to stop fearing them)<br /> <br /> Yet, as it has been noted the PC (that usually start as less than Neonates) likely will get smashed by anyone with a few lvl 5 Disciplines and BP, that's also smart enough to not get into their traps (as any elder should be).<br /> <br /> That's a problem in itself, because Elders deserving of the title weren't &quot;anyone&quot;. They represented a power gap that couldn't get surmounted by XP alone, that could scare even Princes. That Helena isn't much above lesser elders, not really, it's a problem in itself for the narrative. Perhaps a bigger problem than being above the PC! - you see lot's of people being able to do the same as her, even if you yourself are trash and can't. Then why is she such a big deal for the Vampiric world? - Merely nerfing (even more) the PC doesn't solve this, you have to nerf the whole world (more than what V5 already does, judging from what people says about Horatio) OR make a house-rule<br /> <br /> It has been suggested that you could tie Generation to Disciplines, and allow more than 5 powers for low gens. I think that alone can be a huge step towards making Elders scary again. Being able to order mass suicide (and similar) it's above ordering the masses and having absolute control of only one person. And being creatives here, one could always invent Amalgams to reach power levels above what's in the Basic. Between these two, I think you can have elders almost as scary as those of the days of yore w/o breaking anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 08-13-2020, 12:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T09:42:44-07:00","id":1407965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KarlB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401610-how-do-you-express-elder-traits-disciplines-in-v5?p=1407940#post1407940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That's actually the case RAW. XP gain is a bit lower than previous editions, and XP costs are noticeably higher. It takes a lot longer for PCs to reach elder like powers now. So overall, power levels are lower across the board.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You give the players <i>less </i>than the 1-2 xp per session that V5 grant's them <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I actually play and moderate in a 24/7 server where you could get 30 XP a month before we balanced it. I created an entire powerpoint on how we had to balance it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Storyteller of Boston by Night on Twitch <a href=\"https://www.twitch.tv/theonyxpath\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.twitch.tv/theonyxpath</a><br /> Fan of WOD Since 2013","edited":{"userid":26354,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26354-michelleclight","user":"MichelleCLight","date":".  added information to clarify 08-13-2020, 12:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26354-michelleclight","name":"MichelleCLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26354_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T10:15:40-07:00","id":1407972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KarlB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401610-how-do-you-express-elder-traits-disciplines-in-v5?p=1407938#post1407938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Please note that</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes, we understood the first time. You're repeating yourself without stating anything new. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So in reality, the only real difference is they don't have these crazy 6+ dot discipline powers, but on the other hand, 5 dot powers in V5 are overall stronger than 5 dot powers of old ... Player characters themselves pretty much never had access to these insane powers as PCs were generally capped at 8th gen and it's 5 dot limit. . </div> </div> </div>It seems you need to be schooled. <br /> <br /> 5th level powers are , perhaps, stronger. But &quot;please note that...&quot; <br /> 1st level powers are weaker<br /> 2nd level powers are weaker<br /> 3rd level powers are weaker<br /> 4th level powers are weaker. <br /> <br /> Player characters have far less access to 'insane powers' than they did before. A good example; What once was a single level of auspex now needs three levels of Auspex, and because you're using three levels of auspex to match what was once level 1 you've essentially slain half your potential; Aura perception? Do you want that as a fourth level power? Spirit's touch? is that 4th? You want the first three levels of old Auspex you're going to end up using five levels of auspex and have no space for power four and... Hey look, V5's 5th level auspex powers are way weaker; None of these compare to Astral projection. <br /> <br /> Dominate? not as extreme but pretty devestating nerfs; Command isn't much different, mesmorize has about 1/4 the utility, and you have the option of of buying a 1/4th of that utility back with a third level power... but then that would push the all-important forgetful mind up to four. Rationalize wouldn't really be very useful with the old dominate being far more subtle and Terminal decree is an absolute waste of a power (just have the person shot; it's not hard) but the old Dominate 5, possession, was fucking baller so... Are you sure 5th level powers are stronger here? <br /> <br /> Obfuscate; Same shit. Mask of a thousand faces was a third level power and you could look like whoever you wanted with it. That has been pushed up to... was it 4 or 5? That's an absolute game wrecker for several of my characters. <br /> <br /> I don't want to seem like I'm picking on you; I'll grant you presence is stronger now, but that's about it. You really shouldn't be saying such brazenly untrue things. Potence is weak. Celerity is weak. Fortitude is... interesting. Oblivion's a joke. Thaumaturgy's not what it says on the tin. Elders in V5 are just food for any coterie that happens by. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T11:02:40-07:00","id":1407989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401610-how-do-you-express-elder-traits-disciplines-in-v5?p=1407972#post1407972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> was it 4 or 5</div> </div> </div> </div>5.<br /> <br /> In addition to the disciplines you mentioned, what used to be a merit now needs to occupy an entire level of discipline.<br /> <br /> I'm referring to Celerity, Cat's Grace. <br /> <br /> Balance yourself? smh A circus acrobat can do the same. There is nothing supernatural about this ability to balance. <br /> <br /> There is also nothing supernatural about a trained pet, but then you have the first level of animalism... Fifth level of level protean mist form does not represent level 6+. Well, there's the second option where you can take the power that lets you move very slowly while you have a stake through your heart so if SI does not burn or decapitate your body shortly after staking you (how likely is that to happen?), after two hours without any surveillance you can slowly move your hand halfway up to hold the stake in your chest, and if it does not dawn in the the next two hours you can even try to remove the stake. <br /> <br /> If a hunter make your pc enter in torpor by stake on my table, better create another sheet because sadly you have no chance of escaping final death. If you have this power and never suffer torpor by a stake ever after (likely), congratulations your xp was thrown in the trash can. <br /> <br /> Summing up, I am not impressed with what would be the culmination of the disciplines. I think the argument &quot;level 5 powers in v5 are equivalent to powers level 6+ in VtM&quot; does not hold water when inspected more closely. I will not even comment on the fourth level of physical disciplines and Thaum. to avoid being banned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24832,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","user":"blailton","date":". 08-13-2020, 03:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T11:38:52-07:00","id":1407993,"title":"","content":"It would be pretty exciting if there was a new source book in the future for elders, which gives higher leveled powers and maybe even tips on how to play as a kick-ass elder kindred in a chronicle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Storyteller of Boston by Night on Twitch <a href=\"https://www.twitch.tv/theonyxpath\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.twitch.tv/theonyxpath</a><br /> Fan of WOD Since 2013","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26354-michelleclight","name":"MichelleCLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26354_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-21T06:06:55-07:00","id":1409536,"title":"","content":"Running V5 for a 1987 game:<br /> <br /> V5 is a great little system, but essentially it's advertising for the Paradox video games. So everything is video gamey. There's a reason the company that made the first three books doesn't exist anymore. It's a disappointment, but a fixable one. However, I started running it and I don't want to go through the pain in the butt of going back to V20. It takes some doing, and maybe they'll expand the line to the point I don't have to write my own rules, but that Summer 2019 release date on the Player's Guide is not encouraging.<br /> <br /> I run games before 1999 so I don't have to even think about Thinblood Alchemy (just play a ghoul) and the SI. (we already have the Technocracy) 90% of my problems with V5 can be excised with a time jump. <br /> <br /> That also means that the Beckoning hasn't happened yet, so what do we do for the elders?<br /> <br /> - Vampires can learn up to their blood potency in additional Discipline powers at the normal cost after they have 5 dots in a discipline. So a BP 3 Torreador has five dots in Presence and knows Awe, Lingering Kiss, Summoning, and Star Magnetism. That Torrie could learn the remaining powers of Presence up to level 3: Daunt for 5xp, Dread Gaze for 15xp<br /> <br /> -Anyone of Blood Potency 3 or higher can make their own Discipline powers. This, combined with the above, gives a lot of growth room for Blood Sorcery. <br /> <br /> -Whenever someone has a dice pool over ten and uses it, it weakens the local Gauntlet/Consensus/Reality. Any funny rules interactions are caused by this. <br /> <br /> OR<br /> <br /> -Just play V20.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Gogo Baccala<br /> <br /> Drag Queen, Ex-Attorney, Freelance Deity","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26376-gogobaccala","name":"Gogobaccala","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-21T14:34:00-07:00","id":1409627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gogobaccala</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401610-how-do-you-express-elder-traits-disciplines-in-v5?p=1409536#post1409536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Running V5 for a 1987 game:<br /> <br /> V5 is a great little system, but essentially it's advertising for the Paradox video games. So everything is video gamey. There's a reason the company that made the first three books doesn't exist anymore. It's a disappointment, but a fixable one. However, I started running it and I don't want to go through the pain in the butt of going back to V20. It takes some doing, and maybe they'll expand the line to the point I don't have to write my own rules, but that Summer 2019 release date on the Player's Guide is not encouraging.<br /> <br /> I run games before 1999 so I don't have to even think about Thinblood Alchemy (just play a ghoul) and the SI. (we already have the Technocracy) 90% of my problems with V5 can be excised with a time jump.<br /> <br /> That also means that the Beckoning hasn't happened yet, so what do we do for the elders?<br /> <br /> - Vampires can learn up to their blood potency in additional Discipline powers at the normal cost after they have 5 dots in a discipline. So a BP 3 Torreador has five dots in Presence and knows Awe, Lingering Kiss, Summoning, and Star Magnetism. That Torrie could learn the remaining powers of Presence up to level 3: Daunt for 5xp, Dread Gaze for 15xp<br /> <br /> -Anyone of Blood Potency 3 or higher can make their own Discipline powers. This, combined with the above, gives a lot of growth room for Blood Sorcery.<br /> <br /> -Whenever someone has a dice pool over ten and uses it, it weakens the local Gauntlet/Consensus/Reality. Any funny rules interactions are caused by this.<br /> <br /> OR<br /> <br /> -Just play V20.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The company still exists though. It's just no longer operating without Paradox's direct oversight as a self-managed subsidiary. White Wolf is still a thing, with most all the same staff, barring those that left or were fired, like Tobias or Martin. WW as a company manages the WoD IP and brand for Paradox as a managed subsidiary. And WW was always going to farm out all the writing, except the core books; they were up front about this. The only thing that changed is their timetable on it was moved up, and they aren't doing core books in house now. <br /> <br /> As far as that date, anyone looking at it should have know that it was a placeholder, considering they got the license like 3 months beforehand. Modiphius, however, is not like OPP in that they give weekly updates; they send out a weekly email but it only addresses products immediately releasing, current promotions, and such things like that. They have at least answered some emails and FB questions, specifically after they did their closed playtest of the PG material. And we know from interviews that some stuff was kicked back for rewrites. That, coupled with Martin finally being let go and the time it took them to hire their new Brand Creative Manager, Justin Achilli, adds to the lag time. Plus the pandemic. <br /> <br /> At any rate, as of last message someone had from Modiphius, they're currently awaiting some decisions from Paradox regarding it, based on screenshots we've been given of the messages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-22T05:03:42-07:00","id":1409735,"title":"","content":"Yes, yes, White Wolf isn't just the advertising wing of a video game company. How silly of me. I also hear they took Ken Hite to a farm outside of town. And that he gets to run and play and enjoy the outside all he wants.<br /> <br /> <br /> With that said, my V5 game has Elders. You just need to teardown all the bad stuff that they put in to make it a video game tie-in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Gogo Baccala<br /> <br /> Drag Queen, Ex-Attorney, Freelance Deity","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26376-gogobaccala","name":"Gogobaccala","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-22T05:43:31-07:00","id":1409744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401610-how-do-you-express-elder-traits-disciplines-in-v5?p=1402201#post1402201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When Gehenna came out, the book considered Ventrue Antediluvian to be slain right after the Second City, which raised more flame than questions since the writers answers were &quot;errr.... he is beyond life and death&quot; which didn't made sense at all. An &quot;oops, we forgot about Mithras, Alexander and many more embrace dates&quot; would have been better instead of justifying with a lame improvised plot device (that is still being sustained!). Since this things happened before, I rather wait and see that V5 is above such carelessness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mithras is a vampire that has based his undead existence on impersonating a god, a sun god, for millenia.<br /> He lies. He <b><i>always </i></b>lies. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-23T16:05:31-07:00","id":1409972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401610-how-do-you-express-elder-traits-disciplines-in-v5?p=1409744#post1409744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mithras is a vampire that has based his undead existence on impersonating a god, a sun god, for millenia.<br /> He lies. He <b><i>always </i></b>lies. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Cainites ALWAYS lie, but pretty convenient in this particular case when both Dark Ages revised and Victorian Age lines stated that it really was the Ventrue Antediluvian who embraced Mithras. Do you really think that, I quote Gehenna, &quot;this is the secret document that has hidden deep within a file folder at the back of a cabinet for years, these are the 'official' statuses of the members of the Third Generation.&quot; was the ongoing original idea for the metaplot since it all started? I still remember the massive disappointment when that book came out.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-23T22:00:05-07:00","id":1410013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401610-how-do-you-express-elder-traits-disciplines-in-v5?p=1409972#post1409972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Cainites ALWAYS lie, but pretty convenient in this particular case when both Dark Ages revised and Victorian Age lines stated that it really was the Ventrue Antediluvian who embraced Mithras. Do you really think that, I quote Gehenna, &quot;this is the secret document that has hidden deep within a file folder at the back of a cabinet for years, these are the 'official' statuses of the members of the Third Generation.&quot; was the ongoing original idea for the metaplot since it all started? I still remember the massive disappointment when that book came out.</div> </div> </div> </div>But Mithras still takes the lying game to a whole different level on sheer brazeness. If there's someone i can see claiming (false) direct descent of the antediluvian of his clan to the point of using his (dead, possibly diablerized) sire's name for the Founder, because why the helll not, it's him. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I completely ignored Gehenna and still do. Once made a chronicle about some of the Antediluvians returning - and <b>doing absolutely nothing</b> beside chilling with some new kindred out of ennui and curiosity and kindred society going into all kind of hoops, loops, shenanigans and conspiring from trying to process this. Kind of inspired by Ascension of Caine, but without the &quot;it's all a gonzo setite plot, for the evulz&quot; cheap reveal &amp; ending.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 08-24-2020, 01:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-23T22:40:12-07:00","id":1410015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401610-how-do-you-express-elder-traits-disciplines-in-v5?p=1410013#post1410013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But Mithras still takes the lying game to a whole different level on sheer brazeness. If there's someone i can see claiming (false) direct descent of the antediluvian of his clan to the point of using his (dead, possibly diablerized) sire's name for the Founder, because why the helll not, it's him. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I completely ignored Gehenna and still do. Once made a chronicle about some of the Antediluvians returning - and <b>doing absolutely nothing</b> beside chilling with some new kindred out of ennui and curiosity and kindred society going into all kind of hoops, loops, shenanigans and conspiring from trying to process this. Kind of inspired by Ascension of Caine, but without the &quot;it's all a gonzo setite plot, for the evulz&quot; cheap reveal &amp; ending.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Again, the whole lines of Dark Ages revised and Victorian Age stated that Mithras is not lying. The false claim of descent from Antediluvian was due to the misunderstood generation of Maltheas in TC2, which states as 5th (pg. 99), but he actually is 4th (explained in pg. 67). Whoever wrote the book should clarified that the stats in the NPC section were what the kindred there appeared to be, not the real ones (like Hardestadt, who is 6th and appears to be 5th).<br /> <br /> Current writers are bent on modifying the metaplot history to their liking ignoring many of what stated to be canon before and one of the things they seem to tease about is that Mithras was not embraced by the Antediluvian (or that the 3rd generation Ventrue who embraced Mithras was not the original clan founder in an attempt to retcon the &quot;Ventrue is dead a long time ago&quot; mess from Gehenna), choosing to ignore all the previous editions.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1594,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","user":"Saga","date":". 08-24-2020, 01:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-23T23:12:08-07:00","id":1410018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Necroticbinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401610-how-do-you-express-elder-traits-disciplines-in-v5?p=1402256#post1402256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So. Plot devices, which are absolutely irrelevant to the game mechanics and can be represented as just that. But. Mithras can still command his entire blood line with a thought. For example: Ancestral Dominion is a Dominate 4, Blood Sorcery 3 amalgam that let's you dominate a descendant at any distance. It does admittedly not work if the vampire's defense pool goes above 10 but, Mithras might have a more powerful version of something like that. (That power is literally from the cult of Mithras) Mithras also at full strength would have BP 9 or 10. This means that even if he had a stamina of 1, he'd still have a health pool of 9. He could activate toughness for almost free, he can sling around Defy bane again, for almost free as well as Flesh of Marble. If he activated all of those powers, he'd have spent on average a whole 1 hunger.<br /> <br /> The Montano thing would be fitting for a ceremony given that Shadow Step is literally already a power, and so a Ceremony that extends it from &amp;quot;Line of Sight&amp;quot; to &amp;quot;Anywhere in the world&amp;quot; would fit within the power level and scope of the game.<br /> <br /> Ur-Shulgi and Al-Ashrad were... plot devices that weren't really represented in game anyways. In game terms, they'd have a minimum BP of 5 but more than likely have much more. Still, that BP of 5 means they get a minimum of 3 dice on every discipline, and can add three more at a whim. If they were max power, that goes up to 5 for the minimum and 5 for a surge. That means that they could have a pool of 20 with the barest of effort. Which in this system is pretty highly overkill<br /> <br /> Again, a plot point for the dragon thing. But something that would be doable as a max level power and or loresheet.<br /> <br /> Yes, a neonate can do these things. IF they know that it exists, IF they cultivate their blood that way, and IF they were to grow in that way.<br /> <br /> At the least, Thaumaturgy has always been represented as being able to do everything that everyone else can do. It's literally noted as being a highly flexible paradigm.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the rules don't support an action it cannot be done, plus those Meths you describe are vastly nerfed even at 20dice, it doesn't matter that they can Slaughter a coeterie, it matters if they have the power to break nations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-25T02:14:24-07:00","id":1410252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gogobaccala</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401610-how-do-you-express-elder-traits-disciplines-in-v5?p=1409536#post1409536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Running V5 for a 1987 game:<br /> <br /> V5 is a great little system, but essentially it's advertising for the Paradox video games. So everything is video gamey. There's a reason the company that made the first three books doesn't exist anymore. It's a disappointment, but a fixable one. However, I started running it and I don't want to go through the pain in the butt of going back to V20. It takes some doing, and maybe they'll expand the line to the point I don't have to write my own rules, but that Summer 2019 release date on the Player's Guide is not encouraging.<br /> <br /> I run games before 1999 so I don't have to even think about Thinblood Alchemy (just play a ghoul) and the SI. (we already have the Technocracy) 90% of my problems with V5 can be excised with a time jump.<br /> <br /> That also means that the Beckoning hasn't happened yet, so what do we do for the elders?<br /> <br /> - Vampires can learn up to their blood potency in additional Discipline powers at the normal cost after they have 5 dots in a discipline. So a BP 3 Torreador has five dots in Presence and knows Awe, Lingering Kiss, Summoning, and Star Magnetism. That Torrie could learn the remaining powers of Presence up to level 3: Daunt for 5xp, Dread Gaze for 15xp<br /> <br /> -Anyone of Blood Potency 3 or higher can make their own Discipline powers. This, combined with the above, gives a lot of growth room for Blood Sorcery.<br /> <br /> -Whenever someone has a dice pool over ten and uses it, it weakens the local Gauntlet/Consensus/Reality. Any funny rules interactions are caused by this.<br /> <br /> OR<br /> <br /> -Just play V20.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would say just play V20.<br /> <br /> V5 is more than just a new rule system, it's a re-invention of Vampire the Masquerade with a focus on progressing the timeline and while certainly its based and includes all of the classic history of Vampire The Masquerade, it does it with a casual hand wave. Which simply means that, the relevance of kindred history in a modern day V5 chronicle is really not important or that relevant to the game.<br /> <br /> If your goal is to run a traditional 99 Masquerade Chronicle with Elders etc... in the V20 timeline, it will be easier I think to run V20 game and pull your favorite mechanical systems from V5 to V20, then it is going to be to do it the other way around.<br /> <br /> I think V5 is a great system, if you use it in the way its designed to be used, which is to run a modern day chronicle in an era of the second inquisition, the Beckoning etc. You sort of have to buy into the history/setting being presented for the rules to be aligned, else you run into these difficult to explain concepts. Now of course in the hands of a highly motivated GM comfertable with creating/managing rules, its certainly doable, but again, I'm not sure its worth the effort. V20 is a great system for a great game and like V5, V20 has a very specific world/setting assumption built into it, if you are going to run a chronicle that focuses on that setting, you may as well run V20 if you ask me. No reason to overcomplicate things, the important thing is that you create a great game/story for your players, which system you use is ... well it shouldn't be the main thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24511-xguild","name":"xguild","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-25T13:11:22-07:00","id":1410376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xguild</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401610-how-do-you-express-elder-traits-disciplines-in-v5?p=1410252#post1410252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I would say just play V20.<br /> <br /> V5 is more than just a new rule system, it's a re-invention of Vampire the Masquerade with a focus on progressing the timeline and while certainly its based and includes all of the classic history of Vampire The Masquerade, it does it with a casual hand wave. Which simply means that, the relevance of kindred history in a modern day V5 chronicle is really not important or that relevant to the game.<br /> <br /> If your goal is to run a traditional 99 Masquerade Chronicle with Elders etc... in the V20 timeline, it will be easier I think to run V20 game and pull your favorite mechanical systems from V5 to V20, then it is going to be to do it the other way around.<br /> <br /> I think V5 is a great system, if you use it in the way its designed to be used, which is to run a modern day chronicle in an era of the second inquisition, the Beckoning etc. You sort of have to buy into the history/setting being presented for the rules to be aligned, else you run into these difficult to explain concepts. Now of course in the hands of a highly motivated GM comfertable with creating/managing rules, its certainly doable, but again, I'm not sure its worth the effort. V20 is a great system for a great game and like V5, V20 has a very specific world/setting assumption built into it, if you are going to run a chronicle that focuses on that setting, you may as well run V20 if you ask me. No reason to overcomplicate things, the important thing is that you create a great game/story for your players, which system you use is ... well it shouldn't be the main thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I hadn't started with V5 2 years ago assuming that I'd at least have 13 clans and an actual interesting metaplot by now, I would still be using V20. I was a playtester for V5, I ran it at Gen Con as part of the release. I believed in V5 and I wanted to run it. I defended V5 endlessly online and in real life. After 2 years of wondering where the rest of it is, I'm jaded because I had to finish it myself.<br /> <br /> Now I'm running V5 out of spite, with home brew Paths of Enlightenment, Koldunism, and a full library of PC made Thaumaturgy. The Second Inquisition is absolutely a Technocracy plot to remove the Reality Deviant Kindred as competing manipulators of humanity.<br /> <br /> A few of my players tried joining other V5 games and immediately quit because the world was so boring and limited. That's a feature, not a bug: I run V5 the way I do to make every other V5 game feel lacking. I took the video game advertisement that they charged me money for and made it good. <br /> <br /> So yes, if you're sane and not personally invested in this like I am, just play V20.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Gogo Baccala<br /> <br /> Drag Queen, Ex-Attorney, Freelance Deity","edited":{"userid":26376,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26376-gogobaccala","user":"Gogobaccala","date":". 08-25-2020, 04:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26376-gogobaccala","name":"Gogobaccala","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-25T14:35:56-07:00","id":1410397,"title":"","content":"V20 elder disciplines <i>do</i> need a lot of work. <br /> <br /> -I don't think Celerity/Fortitude/Potence should have any suggested 6+ powers (some of them don't even particularly fit with how the discipline metaphysically works) I just think you should get a cool list of what kind of feats you can do with higher and higher physical disciplines; Being able to make handholds out of walls shouldn't be it's own power, it should just be something you do at potence 6. <br /> <br /> Most Discipline descriptions for levels 8/9 should be vague anecdotes and theories rather than fully stated items, except for when you can make a story out of it (a whole city going mad). But levels 6 and 7 should remain because your city's elders are likely to have them and they're great goals to have players work towards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-25T16:25:21-07:00","id":1410425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gogobaccala</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401610-how-do-you-express-elder-traits-disciplines-in-v5?p=1410376#post1410376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If I hadn't started with V5 2 years ago assuming that I'd at least have 13 clans and an actual interesting metaplot by now, I would still be using V20. I was a playtester for V5, I ran it at Gen Con as part of the release. I believed in V5 and I wanted to run it. I defended V5 endlessly online and in real life. After 2 years of wondering where the rest of it is, I'm jaded because I had to finish it myself.<br /> <br /> Now I'm running V5 out of spite, with home brew Paths of Enlightenment, Koldunism, and a full library of PC made Thaumaturgy. The Second Inquisition is absolutely a Technocracy plot to remove the Reality Deviant Kindred as competing manipulators of humanity.<br /> <br /> A few of my players tried joining other V5 games and immediately quit because the world was so boring and limited. That's a feature, not a bug: I run V5 the way I do to make every other V5 game feel lacking. I took the video game advertisement that they charged me money for and made it good.<br /> <br /> So yes, if you're sane and not personally invested in this like I am, just play V20.</div> </div> </div> </div>V5 is a remake of the original Vampire the Masquerade, a game created and updated between 91 and 11, which is 20 years of development. V5 has been out officially for 2 years as of August. Its safe to say that its going to take some time for V5 to catch up to its predecessor and realistically it probably never will given that the era of creating mass splat books has come and gone a long time ago.<br /> <br /> I would not have expected V5 to be pumping out books any faster then it is now. I think you can safely assume you will never see clan books and you might get 1-3 books a year if we are lucky.<br /> <br /> The business has changed, the market has changed, the people playing games have changed. There is no developer on earth and no design of Vampire The Masquerade that could be created that would satisfy the nostalgia this community craves.<br /> <br /> The problem is not that the game has changed, or that books aren't being being pumped out fast enough or that there is no interesting meta plot or that the rules are bad or any of that. The problem is that its not 20 years ago and we, the fans of the original are not our 20 years ago selves.<br /> <br /> I have a group of friends that I tried running a V20 game for, after we had run a V5 campaign, just to see how they liked the difference. I believe the best quote I got from them was that &quot;they like the original Vampire The Masquerade better&quot;, but they where referring to V5. Different game, for a different time for a different gaming culture. What can you do, it is what it is.<br /> <br /> Personally I'm sold on V5. I'm on my second chronicle now after a brief pause with the same group and its an absolute smash hit and frankly, my players who never played the original Vampire have no idea what is and isn't missing. They know V5, to them, that's the game, they don't really know the rich culture and history of White Wolf Games, their first introduction into this world is through V5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24511,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24511-xguild","user":"xguild","date":". 08-25-2020, 07:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24511-xguild","name":"xguild","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-26T01:08:03-07:00","id":1410466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xguild</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401610-how-do-you-express-elder-traits-disciplines-in-v5?p=1410425#post1410425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> V5 is a remake of the original Vampire the Masquerade, a game created and updated between 91 and 11, which is 20 years of development. V5 has been out officially for 2 years as of August. Its safe to say that its going to take some time for V5 to catch up to its predecessor and realistically it probably never will given that the era of creating mass splat books has come and gone a long time ago.<br /> <br /> I would not have expected V5 to be pumping out books any faster then it is now. I think you can safely assume you will never see clan books and you might get 1-3 books a year if we are lucky.<br /> <br /> The business has changed, the market has changed, the people playing games have changed. There is no developer on earth and no design of Vampire The Masquerade that could be created that would satisfy the nostalgia this community craves.<br /> <br /> The problem is not that the game has changed, or that books aren't being being pumped out fast enough or that there is no interesting meta plot or that the rules are bad or any of that. The problem is that its not 20 years ago and we, the fans of the original are not our 20 years ago selves.<br /> <br /> I have a group of friends that I tried running a V20 game for, after we had run a V5 campaign, just to see how they liked the difference. I believe the best quote I got from them was that &amp;quot;they like the original Vampire The Masquerade better&amp;quot;, but they where referring to V5. Different game, for a different time for a different gaming culture. What can you do, it is what it is.<br /> <br /> Personally I'm sold on V5. I'm on my second chronicle now after a brief pause with the same group and its an absolute smash hit and frankly, my players who never played the original Vampire have no idea what is and isn't missing. They know V5, to them, that's the game, they don't really know the rich culture and history of White Wolf Games, their first introduction into this world is through V5.</div> </div> </div> </div>Everyone likes different things. Some people like lutefisk. I have no animosity to lovers of lutefisk.<br /> <br /> But I'm not going to pretend I like it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Gogo Baccala<br /> <br /> Drag Queen, Ex-Attorney, Freelance Deity","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26376-gogobaccala","name":"Gogobaccala","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-26T01:56:35-07:00","id":1410476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gogobaccala</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401610-how-do-you-express-elder-traits-disciplines-in-v5?p=1410466#post1410466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Everyone likes different things. Some people like lutefisk. I have no animosity to lovers of lutefisk.<br /> <br /> But I'm not going to pretend I like it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ah in that case you must be a Swede by my estimation. I can't say I have any animosity to eaters of lutefisk, but eeesh, I think I rather eat surstromming!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24511-xguild","name":"xguild","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-28T15:27:34-07:00","id":1410893,"title":"","content":"Not a Swede. I just know the taste of old lye fish. <br /> <br /> &quot;OTHER ERAS <br /> By default, Vampire is set tonight, right now.<br /> However, nothing stops you from running a chronicle that starts its clock in 1991, 1968, 1888, 1204 or in ancient Rome 120 AD. While this book doesn\u2019t have full rules or setting sup-port for historical chronicles \u2013 and obviously no edition could ever cover all of Kindred his-tory \u2013 older editions and versions have plenty, most notably Victorian Age Vampire and Vampire: The Dark Ages.&quot;<br /> <br /> Pg. 139, Core rules.<br /> <br /> We didn't make a full game. But use our good books we used to make if you want useful material.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-div